      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.07-01",
      "block_type": "definition",
      "heading": "Latitude, longitude and angular units",
      "text": "Latitude gives angular position north or south of the Equator, while longitude gives angular position east or west of the prime meridian. Latitude is conventionally stated before longitude in the coordinate pairs used here. Include the hemisphere or a clearly defined signed convention. A coordinate without its direction can identify more than one possible location.",
