      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.07-04",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "For example, 23°01′30″ south is 23 + 1/60 + 30/3,600 = 23.025 degrees south. A signed decimal convention expresses it as −23.025°. Writing −23.025°S would mix conventions unnecessarily, so state the convention clearly. The number 23.0130 is not the decimal conversion of that DMS coordinate.",
