    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.07-05",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A teaching coordinate panel can mark P at 23°00′30″S,17°00′30″E and Q at 23°01′30″S,17°01′30″E. Q is one minute farther south and one minute farther east in angular terms. Their midpoint in this local angular exercise is 23°01′00″S,17°01′00″E. The latitude and longitude differences are not automatically equal ground distances.\n\n![Coordinate panel with P, Q and midpoint M](../../assets/images/ITEM-6137-4.2-034-INTERP-answer.png)",
