    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.07-06",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "In the Southern Hemisphere, a larger south latitude value is farther from the Equator and therefore farther south. A smaller south value is farther north. In the Eastern Hemisphere, increasing east longitude is eastward. Read the labelled graticule rather than assuming that numbers always increase towards the top or the right under every projection or orientation.",
