    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.07-07",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "To locate a point, use the latitude and longitude lines or interpolate within their stated intervals. Keep both coordinates and hemispheres. If a point lies halfway between 23°00′S and 23°01′S, its latitude is 23°00′30″S under the local interpolation used. Estimate to the precision supported by the resource rather than inventing seconds from a coarse grid.",
