      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.07-08",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Angular differences are not ordinary map lengths. A minute of longitude represents different east–west ground distances at different latitudes, while a map projection also affects representation. For the distance tasks here, use the stated 1:50,000 scale and compatible map measurements. The coordinate task identifies position; it should not silently convert one minute into one kilometre.",
