      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.07-09",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Arithmetic crossing a minute or degree boundary uses base sixty. Adding twenty seconds of southward latitude to 23°59′50″S gives 24°00′10″S: the first ten seconds reach the next degree and ten remain. Hemisphere and direction still matter. If the movement were northward, the south magnitude would decrease instead.",
