    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.07-10",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A map's rectangular kilometre grid and its latitude/longitude graticule are different systems. Eastings and northings are linear coordinates in a projection, while latitude/longitude are angular positions. Do not assign a centimetre distance to a degree label without the appropriate conversion. A well-prepared resource can show both consistently, with the key or marginal labels identifying which is used for each task.",
