    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.07-12",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A decimal-to-DMS check reverses the process. For 17.025 degrees east, the whole degrees are seventeen. Multiplying the remaining 0.025 by sixty gives 1.5 minutes, so there is one whole minute and half a minute left. Half a minute is thirty seconds. The result is 17°01′30″E. This arithmetic uses base sixty at each stage rather than simply reading the decimal digits as minutes and seconds.",
      "claim_ids": [
