    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.07-13",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Angular subtraction can require borrowing. Between 23°00′30″S and 23°01′30″S the difference is one minute, with the second point farther south. Between 23°00′50″S and 23°01′10″S, the difference is twenty seconds: ten to reach the next minute and ten more. A written subtraction can borrow sixty seconds from a minute. Retain the hemisphere before describing the direction.",
