    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.07-15",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A map projection translates the curved Earth onto a flat surface and can represent directions, areas or distances with particular properties. The learner does not need to design that projection for these tasks, but should respect the labels and scale. A rectangular grid drawn for linear measurement should not be given arbitrary degree labels as if the systems were identical. The map's coordinate framework must support both consistently.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-4.2.07-1",
        "CL-6137-4.2.07-2",
        "CL-6137-4.2.07-01-1",
        "CL-6137-4.2.07-01-2",
